cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use eleman, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "eleman: a personal memory core for AI assistants"
authors:
  - family-names: Akadal
    given-names: Emre
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6817-0127"
    affiliation: "Istanbul University"
abstract: >-
  eleman is a repository that an AI assistant reads and writes as its long-term
  memory: plain markdown files, a directory convention, a few standard-library
  scripts and git underneath. New information enters through an append-only
  inbox and is distilled into small, budgeted domain files by a periodic
  consolidation run. It needs no service, database or API key, and works with
  any agent that can read files.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23975338
repository-code: "https://github.com/akadal/eleman"
url: "https://eleman.akadal.tr"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - AI assistants
  - large language models
  - context window
  - personal knowledge management
  - markdown
